## The Ostwick Gate

::bg{location="ostwick_gate" time="dawn"}
::music{action="start" mood="upbeat" volume="down"}
@narrator: Eleven wagons, forty mules, and a strongbox nobody is supposed to know about. East of the gate the Ember Road opens like a wound that never closed.
::auto{character="brannoc" anchor="center" action="fadeInUp"}
@brannoc: Warden. The Company has paid for three things: the cargo, the road, and you. Get all eleven wagons over the Tollbridge before the fourth night.
@brannoc: Harrow's Ford is a day out. Past the ford it's Dusk country.
::auto{character="isolde" anchor="left" action="fadeInUp"}
@isolde: The Duskbound are deserters and hungry farmers, Captain. Not demons.
@brannoc: Hungry farmers with crossbows, Vane.
::auto{character="corvin" anchor="right" action="fadeInUp"}
@corvin: And a toll, I hear. Everyone on this road has a toll. Some of us are only more honest about it.

<branch id="orders" prompt="Brannoc waits for your answer.">
  <choice id="swear" label="\"The wagons cross. You have my word.\"">
    @brannoc: Your word. Good. The Company collects on those.
    ::set{run.rep.company += 1}
    ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="approves"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="price" label="For what you pay, the wagons get there. The mules are a maybe.">
    @brannoc: Funny. Get the mules there too.
    ::use{component="reaction" who="corvin" feel="approves"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="dusk" label="What did the Company do to the Duskbound?">
    @brannoc{emotion="angry"}: Nothing they didn't earn. Mind your road, Warden.
    ::set{run.rep.company -= 1}
    ::use{component="reaction" who="isolde" feel="approves"}
    @isolde: A fair question. Notice he didn't answer it.
  </choice>
</branch>

::auto{character="brannoc" action="fadeOut"}
@corvin: Eleven wagons. You know what's in the twelfth crate of the ninth wagon?
@isolde: Corvin.
@corvin: I'm only saying the Company counts to eleven and packs twelve.
@narrator: The gate grinds open. The Ember Road takes you in.
